            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "<table><tr><td colspan=\"2\"></td><td colspan=\"3\">Relevant credentials</td></tr><tr><td>Security appliances</td><td>Comment</td><td>EVCC (EV)</td><td>SECC (EVSE) private SECC (for PE only)</td><td>Secondary actor</td></tr><tr><td>DC/AC charging with PnC with dynamic tariffs, contract key updates and provisioning -DC/AC charging with transport security -contracts based payment, with meter status receipt -individual / dynamic tariff tables for customer -contract certificate installation via EVSE contract certificate validation by SECC</td><td>-TLS authentication of SECC -TLS authentication of EVCC -confidential data exchange between EV and EVSE (service discovery, power delivery, metering) -integrity of data between EV and EVSE (service discovery, power delivery, metering) -integrity of tariff data based on digital signature -integrity of contract keys/certs based on digital signature -confidentiality of private key of new contract certificates based on encryption Appl.Layer: AES for data encryption, ECDH used for key exchange, ECC for digital signature for tariff signing and contract provisioning TLS: AES used for stream/session encryption, ECDH used for key exchange</td><td>Vehicle leaf key pair (vehicle leaf private key and certificate for TLS) certified by a sub-CA which was certified by an OEM root CA or a V2G root CA all vehicle sub-CA certificates of the certificate chain above the vehicle certificate V2G root CA certificate(s) contract key pair (contract private key and certificate for contract based payment) certified by a CA which can be certified by a V2G root CA. all eMSP sub-CA certificates of the certificate chain above the contract certificate OEM prov key pair (OEM prov private key and certificate for contract provisioning) all OEM sub-CA certificate of the certificate chain above the OEM prov certificate</td><td>SECC leaf key pair (up to 10 generations depending on the aging V2G RootKey) (SECC leaf private key and certificate for TLS) certified by a sub-CA which was certified by a V2G root CA all CSO sub-CA certificates of the certificate chain above the SECC OCSP response ticket(s) from the corresponding CSO-sub-CA and V2G root CA OEM root CA certificate(s) (if not below a V2G root. V2G root CA certificate(s) otherwise) all eMSP root CA certificates and V2G root CA certificates of the eMSPs the CSO has contract agreements with.</td><td>eMSP root CA certificate (if not below a V2G root. V2G root CA certificate(s) otherwise) all eMSP-sub-CA certificates of the certificate chain below the eMSP-sub-CA key pair issuing contract certificates eMSP sub-CA key pair (SA private key and certificate) for contract certificate and tariff signing contract key pair to be delivered to the vehicle all prov-sub-CA certificates of the certificate signed by a V2G root (for certificate provisioning service) leaf certificate prov key pair (leaf prov private key and certificate for contract installation/update) certified by a sub-CA which was certified by a V2G root CA (for certificate provisioning service) OEM root CA certificates (if not below a V2G root. V2G root CA certificate(s) otherwise)</td></tr></table>",
